ike  perpetual fall in washington  if that were the case i would  100  no question  right  [Music]  [Laughter]  action  this beautiful rays  but it's also starting to get really  cold  just ate dinner and i'm gonna go set up  my tent  so that once the sun is gone i can just  dive right in and be warm  so pretty  [Music]  [Music]  the light's getting really really good  so  running down to set up my tent  and change into some warmer clothes  out of my hiking pants and stuff like  that and then i'm gonna run back up to  the fire tower lookout and shoot sunset  so here's home for the night just got  all set up  so pretty here  uh  [Music]  oh actually look at that cloud yeah  crazy  [Music]  this is what i admit when i said  they're going off to their tent and i'm  going off to mine  [Laughter]  would you look at that would you look at  that  just look at it  all right so i just hung up my food and  trash  we are in bear country here at mount  rainier national park we've got black  bears around  and  matt and renee are camped over there  and i am camped  down the trail quite a ways  and then i turn off to the right so a  little bit secluded  good morning  the wind is so loud outside  and there's frost on  the tent right now  i do not want to get out of my sleeping  bag but  time to go get the coffee from the bear  bearpole and  head out to go shoot sunrise  i feel like these next few scenes really  mirror what life has been like lately  stumbling around in the dark one step at  a time attempting to create while also  being in the moment  only to realize halfway through that  i've forgotten to turn my mic on which  is why i have music playing instead  like i said i don't know what i'm doing  i'm still learning how to film and what  to film how to stay grounded while  living on the road how to run a business  from the road how to stay happy and  healthy and all of the things  there aren't many road maps out there  explaining how to live as a full-time  nomad long term  especially these days when so many  things feel subject to change  and though i will be the first to say  it's a beautiful way to live it does  come at a cost some days that cost is  overwhelm other days it's a lack of  community lack of stability lack of  clean underwear and sometimes it's just  plain decision fatigue i try to remind  myself that it's okay to be in that  space it's okay to lean into all the  things i don't know and just learn as i  go  choosing the wrong path getting lost and  making mistakes have all been important  parts of my journey guideposts in a way  for me personally it's the challenging  moments that force me to grow the most  and ask myself the deeper questions like  how can i contribute during my time here  on this earth how do i define happiness  and  did i remember to turn the mic on this  time  [Music]  too bad my coffee cup is full of dirt i  actually dropped it in the dirt this  morning  and also because i like coffee and  and i'm sleepy  you guys are such dogs  so i'm all packed up and heading back up  to the lookout  then we're gonna head down the trail and  yeah  it was so cold this morning but it's  starting to get toasty right now this  down jacket's definitely coming off soon  spending time outdoors in nature has  been one of the few constants in my life  since moving on to the road going into  the mountains just it always feels like  going home  being out here just makes me happy and  so often it offers up perspective in  this case a reminder that it's okay to  not know what you're doing  it's okay to spend the day just putting  one foot in front of the other roaming  forested trails picking huckleberries  laughing with friends falling asleep  beneath the stars it's more than okay  it's great it's pretty amazing actually  and i can say with absolute confidence  that i have no idea what comes next  but i'm excited for it anyway thrown in  our bags time to get some food to get  some food  and  as i'm sure you might have guessed 